<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">21032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>On the thirtieth day of war, Israel launched simultaneous airstrikes on Tehran and ground forces into Lebanon, striking two capitals in a single night.</s> <s>Three hundred million people across Iran and Central Asia had gathered to mark <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="noʊˈruːz">Nowruz</phoneme>, the Persian new year, as bombs fell — while Benjamin Netanyahu rejected Donald Trump's personal request to spare Iranian oil infrastructure.</s> <s>The United Arab Emirates told Washington privately to expect nine months of conflict, and the Strait of Hormuz remains closed.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran fired two ballistic missiles at Diego Garcia — the remote island in the Indian Ocean that hosts American B-2 bombers — reaching over three thousand kilometres from Iranian territory, the farthest target Tehran has struck in the war.</s> <s>A United States warship fired an SM-3 interceptor, but the Pentagon has not confirmed whether it made contact.</s> <s>The strike signals that Tehran has already mapped the full reach of American military power in the region.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United Kingdom reversed its policy limiting British bases to defensive use and is now hosting American strikes on Iran.</s> <s>Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɪr ˈstɑːrmər">Keir Starmer</phoneme> changed course after Donald Trump publicly branded North Atlantic Treaty Organization allies cowards — pressure that has visibly reshaped what alliance membership means in practice.</s> <s>Iran's foreign minister warned Starmer that he was putting British lives in danger.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the United States, Georgia prosecutors charged Alexia Moore with murder for taking an abortion pill — the first such prosecution in American history.</s> <s>Georgia's 2022 abortion ban grants fetuses legal personhood, enabling murder charges against women for their own pregnancies.</s> <s>Fourteen other states carry similar statutes, and Camden County prosecutors will decide in coming weeks whether to take the case to trial.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India sent two and a half tonnes of emergency medicine to Kabul, citing Pakistan's strike on a hospital there on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">16032026</say-as> that killed at least four hundred people.</s> <s>New Delhi dispatched the aid despite refusing to recognise the Taliban government, opening a direct humanitarian corridor that bypasses Pakistan entirely.</s> <s>Saudi Arabia, Qatar, and Turkey brokered a five-day Eid ceasefire between Pakistan and Afghanistan that expires at midnight Monday.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Mexican aid convoy carrying fuel and food departed the Yucatan Peninsula on Saturday — the first external relief mission to Cuba since the United States embargo blocked Venezuelan oil shipments last year.</s> <s>Eleven million Cubans lack reliable electricity, and this convoy is the only outside fuel supply Cuba is likely to receive this month.</s> <s>Cuba must authorise the flotilla to dock, or it turns back to Mexico empty.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A federal judge in the United States voided the Pentagon's press credentialing policy, ruling it discriminates based on viewpoint.</s> <s>Judge Paul Friedman found the system had systematically removed critical reporters, replacing them with outlets willing to serve government messaging.</s> <s>The Pentagon has one week to file a compliance report reinstating the credentials it stripped.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israel struck the South Pars gas field this week — the world's largest gas reserve, shared between Iran and Qatar, and the primary source of Qatar's liquefied natural gas exports.</s> <s>Japan sent no executives to China's annual Development Forum for the first time, its government citing the energy emergency; Donald Trump separately invoked Pearl Harbor to pressure Japanese Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈsɑːneɪ tɑːˈkɑɪtʃi">Sanae Takaichi</phoneme>, who has refused to join the coalition on constitutional grounds.</s> <s>South Korean factories are already cutting production shifts as the closure works through Asian supply chains.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington is simultaneously bombing Iran and clearing Iranian oil for global sale — the United States Treasury issued its third thirty-day waiver in two weeks, allowing buyers to purchase one hundred and forty million barrels stranded on tankers.</s> <s>Its purpose is to suppress fuel prices at home, even as American aircraft fly strike missions over Tehran.</s> <s>The waiver expires on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">19042026</say-as>, and the Treasury has not said whether it will be renewed.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The International Energy Agency has called the Hormuz closure the largest oil supply disruption on record, and Asian utilities are responding by returning to coal.</s> <s>Agency reserves total one and a half billion barrels — but those stocks were designed for short disruptions, not a conflict now projected to last nine months.</s> <s>The European Commission must decide this summer whether to overhaul its emissions trading system as the energy crisis overtakes its climate commitments.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Scientists have found that a species of jellyfish keeps time without any of the clock genes shared by nearly all other animals.</s> <s>The hydrozoan evolved an independent twenty-hour timer, suggesting that biological timekeeping has more than one evolutionary origin.</s> <s>Researchers are now studying how the jellyfish synchronizes to sunlight without the molecular machinery that makes that possible in every other known animal.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>South Korea's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tʃʌŋ.ɡʊŋ">Cheongung</phoneme>-II missile interceptor hit ninety-six percent of its targets in its combat debut in the United Arab Emirates — the first time a non-American system has been tested against real incoming fire.</s> <s>Seoul built it at one third the cost of a Patriot battery, after Washington's pricing made full coverage of the North Korean threat unaffordable.</s> <s>Raytheon now faces its first serious competition in the fifty billion dollar global missile defense market.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A tool presented at the German Perl Workshop can automatically parallelize old Perl code to run on multiple processor cores, with no modifications to the programs themselves.</s> <s>Perl, a programming language that peaked in the nineteen-nineties but still underpins significant infrastructure worldwide, has never had a tool that speeds up existing code without rewriting it.</s> <s>The tool's creator has not yet released the source code.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>